      "writtenOn": "2021-05-30T10:53:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is going back and forth few times now.\nThis worker is being scheduled repeatedly from itself,  but also on resume.\nOriginally, I had this protection because I was scheduling this worker using different timeouts.\nDaejun made a similar comment like yours on the mainline\u0027s v4, so I removed it on my v5.\n\nOn v5, CanG commented that since I am not protecting the expired_list, \"If two\nread_to_handler works are running in parallel, one can be inserting it to its expired_list while another can be deleting it.\"\nMy answer was: \"The timeout handler, being a delayed work, is meant to run every polling period.  Originally, I had it protected from 2 handlers running concurrently, But I removed it following Daejun\u0027s comment, which I accepted, Since it is always scheduled using the same polling period.\"\n\nBut then CanG made a winning argument: \"But one can set the delay to 0 through sysfs, right?\"\n\nSo I put that protection on.  What do you think?\n\nThanks.",
      "parentUuid": "766e5f6e_f07401f9",
